# wfg-log 1
# fixture eq - a media cue's EQ written while a show runs (Phase 9a, PR 9a.2).
#
# WHAT IT IS FOR: that a session in which a rotary, a panel or the page wrote
# a media cue's EQ rows - decisions about the show, through the document's own
# door - then put the whole EQ back with eq.reset and took that back with
# undo, reproduces exactly. Recorded from a real `wfg serve` of
# tests/fixtures/bundles/eq driven over OSC with no audio device; the header
# lines below are the session's own.
#
# bundle eq sha256:16df414a4346597f1e28aefdc27357122667d4211b3cf73d672a143b4fc804f8
# clock sampleRate=48000 blockSize=128 samplesPerTick=960
# media tones.wav 0 0.000
#
# THREE ROWS WRITTEN, one address each: band two moved to a kilohertz and
# lifted six decibels, then the high-pass switched in - a T row, carried as
# the T atom. Each is an ordinary node.set on a persist=show row; nothing
# stands in front of the document for these, unlike a trim.
A 1 0 udp:127.0.0.1:50596 node.set s:"/godot/cue/EQ000002/eqB2Freq" f:1000
A 14 1 udp:127.0.0.1:50596 node.set s:"/godot/cue/EQ000002/eqB2Gain" f:6
A 26 2 udp:127.0.0.1:50596 node.set s:"/godot/cue/EQ000002/eqHpf" T
#
# THE FLAT BUTTON: eq.reset is one command over nineteen rows, so it is one
# transaction on the show's history - which the undo below takes back whole.
# The fixture's own -20 dB band three goes to nought here too.
A 39 3 udp:127.0.0.1:50596 eq.reset s:"EQ000002"
#
# AND ITS UNDO, by the transaction's name: band three is -20 dB again, and the
# three writes above stay - they were three transactions of their own.
A 52 4 udp:127.0.0.1:50596 undo s:"document" s:"eq.reset"
